      "message": "Do we not get the state change from the audio framework as a result of our request? I want to make sure we\u0027re not getting double events.\n\nAs well, I wonder if we can get a race between lines 263 and here where we gain focus from the request, the audio stack knows it, but then we quickly/immediately lose it. They invoked our listener, which puts an event on our state machine for a loss, but then we manually trigger the listener with a gain and now we *think* we have focus when we don\u0027t because we process loss, then gain, on our handler.\n\nIf that\u0027s the case, it might just be better to execute `startFlourideStreaming()` as we did, and invoked AVRCP\u0027s callback her einstead. That way we can guarantee the order of events.\n\nDefinitely set mAudioFocus first too, despite what the old code did. Starting streaming could give us a PLAYING state in AVRCP potentially before the focus is set, which could cause us to pause when we don\u0027t actually mean to.",
